Could you have a look? This is some explanation:
Buffer/path | Effect of the prototype
-- | --
Decompressed pages and decoder state | Still buffer-managed, unpinned between reads, and evictable
Compressed-page temporaries and footer buffer | These already stay pinned until destruction; changing allocator removes overhead without losing an existing eviction opportunity
Definition/repetition buffers | These already stay pinned for their lifetime; they retain memory-limit accounting through BufferAllocator
Redundant pins | Removes duplicate acquisition. After an actual unpin, the next read still pins and rebases the decoders

